LLAMABIRD INSTALLATION
======================

Prerequisites
-------------
- Python 3.8 or newer
- Thunderbird or Betterbird with QNote extension
- Ollama running locally


Quick Install
-------------

1. Clone the repository:
   $ git clone git@github.com:rsling/Llamabird.git
   $ cd Llamabird

2. Create Python virtual environment:
   $ python3 -m venv venv

3. Activate virtual environment:
   $ source venv/bin/activate

4. Install dependencies:
   $ pip install -r requirements.txt

5. Run environment discovery:
   $ python3 discover.py

   This creates config.json with your Thunderbird profile paths.

6. Test manual summarization (3 emails):
   $ python3 llamabird.py --limit 3 --no-qnote

   Check that summaries appear in German (default language).

7. Install automatic daemon (optional):
   $ ./install_daemon.sh

8. Start the daemon:
   $ systemctl --user start llamabird

9. Check daemon status:
   $ systemctl --user status llamabird


Done! New emails will now be automatically summarized.


Ollama Model
------------
If discover.py reports that the model is not installed:

$ ollama pull qwen2.5


Logs
----
View daemon logs:
$ journalctl --user -u llamabird -f


Configuration
-------------
All settings are in config.json (auto-generated by discover.py)
